        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353-a2">

                <pb facs="0366" n="1044" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1044"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <p>We received your letters, Nos. 71 and 73, dated the 6th of June, and understood
                    that a short sword, which was stolen when our embassy was in the United States,
                    from one of their attendants, having been recovered, is thereby returned, and we
                    now tender our thanks for the trouble taken in regard to this friendly
                    arrangement.</p>
                <p>It was also stated that his Majesty the President had learned with pleasure that
                    two more of the criminals engaged in the attack on the British legation had been
                    punished, which we immediately reported to his Majesty the Tycoon.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Stated in reply to these two letters, with
                        respect and esteem. <date calendar="gregorian japanese-nengō"
                            when="1862-07-03">The 7th day of the 6th month of the 2d year of Bunkin,
                            (the 3d July, 1862</date>.)</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>WAKISAKA NAKATSAKA NO TAYU.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MIDSUNO IDSUMI NO KAMI.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>ITAKURA SUWO NO KAMI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert H. Pruyn</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States of America,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
